.SH NAME
messq-auth-add - mint one token, print its credential once, store its hash


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmessq auth add [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Mint a fresh credential msq1\fI\fP, append its SHA-256 line to the
--auth-file, and print the credential to stdout EXACTLY ONCE. Nobody can show
it again; if it is lost, remove the line by hand and add anew with the same
id — renaming ids invalidates credentials by design (the hash covers them).
The file keeps mode 0600 and single-line appends leave every prior token
intact. Duplicate ids and duplicate hashes are refused before anything is
written: two ids sharing one credential would make events.actor ambiguous.
Roles are publish, consume and admin — plain sets, no hierarchy — scoped to
comma-separated stream patterns ('orders' is exact, 'orders*' covers the
family including orders.dlq).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--auth-file\fP=""
	token file to append to (or MESSQ_AUTH_FILE)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add

.PP
\fB--id\fP=""
	token id: [a-z0-9][a-z0-9._-]{1,63}

.PP
\fB--roles\fP=""
	comma-separated subset of publish, consume, admin

.PP
\fB--streams\fP=""
	comma-separated stream patterns (exact, prefix*, or *)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--addr\fP="unix:///run/messq/messq.sock"
	daemon address (unix://, http://, https://)

.PP
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	colour: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB--full-ids\fP[=false]
	print full ULIDs instead of abbreviated ones

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="auto"
	output mode: auto|table|json|ndjson

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress narration; data and errors unaffected

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	per-request deadline (0 = none)

.PP
\fB--token-file\fP=""
	file holding the bearer token, mode 0600

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	narrate (-vv dumps each HTTP exchange and the resolved config)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  messq auth add --auth-file /etc/messq/tokens \\
      --id ci-worker --roles publish,consume --streams 'orders*,billing'
.EE


